  "semantic_slots": {
    "objects": {
      "original": "Literal all-N balanced Bool count/card laws, signsum/sqrtN pushforward lambdaN from closed public35 signature; gamma=gaussianReal0,1. Fixed real C2 compact-support f, f², f²logf², (deriv f)² and homogeneous entropy.",
      "reconstructed": "A real function f and its real derivative deriv f; the finite carriers Omega_n = Fin n -> Bool; scaled counting measures mu_n defined using their actual cardinalities; actual signed-sum maps S_n; the fixed Gaussian gamma = gaussianReal 0 1; the three observables f^2, f^2 log(f^2), and (deriv f)^2; their finite and Gaussian Bochner integrals and the displayed entropy expressions.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Public local mu/S/gamma exactly match private countLaw/normalizedSum and parent35 literal pushforward; three actual observers and entropy expression coincide."
    },
    "domains": {
      "original": "Finite configuration spaces, real Borel probability weak convergence, real Bochner integrals. Signed f/zeros allowed. C2 supplies continuous derivative; compact support propagates to derivative, powers and zero-preserving entropy composite.",
      "reconstructed": "f and deriv f have domain and codomain Real. Real has its canonical Borel structure. n ranges over Nat including 0. Each finite observable has domain Fin n -> Bool with canonical finite measurable structure and real codomain; mu_n is a measure on that exact carrier. Gaussian observables are measured on Real. Cardinality scaling lies in ENNReal; signed sums, square roots, logarithms, integrals, entropy values, and limit values lie in Real. gamma is a probability Gaussian of mean 0 and variance NNReal 1.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Real Borel and finite canonical measurable carrier; integrable means genuine Bochner L1. Log integrand may have either sign. Closed compact supports and continuous derivative derived, not supplied."
    },
    "quantifiers": {
      "original": "One actual law family for all N; each fixed compact C2 f gives the three actual-count integral limits along positive successor n+1 and entropy limit. No supplied laws/probability/finite-domain/moment/limit certificates.",
      "reconstructed": "Universally quantify f : Real -> Real with proofs of C2 regularity and compact support. mu, S, and gamma are local definitions, not caller parameters. The finite integrability conjunction is universal in every n : Nat, including 0. Each of the four Tendsto conclusions is a limit of a sequence indexed by n : Nat atTop, with its finite measure and signed sum evaluated at the successor n+1 and with convergence into the real neighborhood filter of the specified Gaussian scalar. No rate, uniform quantifier, variable Gaussian parameter, or further certificate is quantified.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Only f,hf,hs binders. Domains for every naturalN including0; four limit sequences use successorN+1. No existential law/output certificate supplied."
    },
    "assumptions": {
      "original": "Only genuine C2 and HasCompactSupport on f for compact-test extension; all probability/L1/bounded continuity conditions internally derived from actual35 law and mathematical support/continuity APIs. No f>0 or integral f²=1 assumption.",
      "reconstructed": "The only mathematical assumptions are ContDiff Real 2 f (C2 on the whole real line) and HasCompactSupport f (compact closure of the nonzero support). C2 supplies differentiability for deriv. No caller-supplied integrability, positivity, nonzero mass, density normalization, probabilistic law, convergence, or entropy certificate occurs.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Exact C2 plus compact support. No positivity, normalized f, moment, measure/selector, L1 or convergence premise. Probability/law/integrability prerequisites internally obtained."
    },
    "conclusion": {
      "original": "Convergence of squared-function, square-entropy-integrand and derivative-square actual integrals, and homogeneous entropy E f²logf² - (E f²)log(E f²). Not GaussianLSI or a flip-energy limit.",
      "reconstructed": "Conjunction of gamma-integrability of f^2, f^2 log(f^2), and (deriv f)^2; integrability of all three composed with S_n against mu_n for every natural n; scalar convergence atTop of each corresponding successor integral to its gamma integral; and scalar convergence of the successor expression B_(n+1)-A_(n+1) log(A_(n+1)) to B-A log(A). Integrable denotes actual Bochner integrability, and all six types of displayed integrals are Bochner integrals. The logarithmic integrand need not be nonnegative. The conclusion contains no inequality, quantitative rate, convergence of derivatives as functions, or quantified law-convergence claim.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Three Gaussian L1 outputs, allN three finite L1 outputs, three scalar observer limits and homogeneous entropy limit, conjuncts exactly preserved."
    },
    "scopes": {
      "original": "Compact authored analytic prerequisite toward sourceGaussianLSI; SLT bespoke BCF proof may be reused or actual Mathlib ofCompactSupport route separately authored. N0 derivative-square expectation may equal nonzero f'(0)² and is not zero merely because lambda0=dirac0.",
      "reconstructed": "mu_n uses inverse actual finite-carrier cardinality times counting measure; S_n uses the displayed sqrt(n) inverse and actual sum of Bool-selected +1/-1 values. All dimensions, including n=0, are covered only by the finite integrability assertion. At n=0 the carrier is a singleton, the sum is empty, inverse zero equals zero, and S_0 is zero. Limits use positive successor dimensions n+1. gamma remains the single fixed mean-zero variance-one Gaussian. Real.log(0)=0 makes f^2 log(f^2) zero at zeros of f and makes mass times log(mass) zero at zero mass; no exclusion or separate positivity assumption is imposed. All four limits are real scalar limits of the expressions literally displayed.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Authored compact scalar prerequisite for omitted GaussianLSI background; no numbered SPHMC theorem or fullflip4 claim. N0 derivative-energy not zeroed; allzero mass/signedf allowed."
    },
    "constant_dependencies": {
      "original": "Same actual normalization2^-N and inverse sqrtN; fixed variance1 Gaussian. Homogeneous entropy no normalization divisor/positivity premise; xlogx continuous at0. GaussianLSI coefficient2/fullflip factor4 not yet inferred.",
      "reconstructed": "The fixed numerical constants are the signs +1 and -1, mean 0, variance 1, exponent 2, and the successor offset 1. The dimension-dependent normalization is exactly 1/sqrt(n), with the stated zero convention, and the measure scaling is exactly inverse actual carrier cardinality in ENNReal. Integrals depend on f and on their displayed measure and dimension. There is no asserted rate constant, universal inequality constant, hidden parameter, or adjustable Gaussian variance.",
      "relation": "equivalent",
      "evidence": "Inverse actual card=2^-N, sign+/-1, inverse sqrtN, mean0/variance1 Gaussian. No LSI coefficient2 or fullflip4 or rate inferred."
    }
  },
